TASK-173 / TASK-174 runtime harness: the Control+Tab switcher's card for a tab
with a Peek, and the keyboard after a click on the sidebar's tab list.
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task173-174-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    OUT="$PWD/.derived-logs/task173"; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify173 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # wait for the "done" line in $OUT/verify.log (about 40 s), then kill that pid
    git apply -R docs/harness/task173-174-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

It needs the sandbox off and the screen unlocked. At each "SHOT <name>
window=<id>" line the overlay stays up for 3 s: capture it from the shell with
`screencapture -x -o -l <id> shot.png`.

    K1  posted click on another tab's row, then a posted key
    K2  find bar focused, posted click on a row, then a posted key
    K3  nothing focused, posted click on the selected row, then a posted key
    SHOT 1  a tab left with a Peek: its card shows the Peek over a dimmed page
    SHOT 2  the same with the Peek's picture removed: the panel shows a globe
    SHOT 3  the current tab has the Peek presented
    SHOT 4  the Peek closed: no panel

Each K step logs the first responder and the keys each page's keydown listener
received. With the list refusing focus the selected page receives the key;
with the old code first responder is DraggableTableView and no page does.

Launched from a shell the app is not the active application, and a posted
click then does not change the list's selection (the K steps all stay on the
first tab). Whether it does in an active application (launched with `open -n`
and no `-g`) was not tried.

